      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on maximizing quality life years and probability of stability, the ranking should be: Patient B, Patient D, Patient A, and Patient C. Patient B offers the highest potential for long-term quality life years due to youth and excellent health. Patient D is next, benefiting from a younger age and professional role suggesting good long-term stability. Patient A is prioritized over C due to their younger age and urban integration, offering more potential years saved. Patient C has the lowest ranking as the combination of advanced age and pre-existing conditions like COPD lowers the probability of long-term success.",
